PLAIN-LANGUAGE SUMMARY (not part of the binding text; if it differs, Sections 1 to 15 win)

  1. You can read, run, copy, change and share this for free if you are not making money
     with it.
  2. If you, or anyone you work for, make money with it, save money with it, or run it as
     part of a for-profit operation, you need a Commercial License. Licensor takes a share
     of the revenue. This applies in every country.
  3. This covers the code AND the architectural specifications and documents. Building a
     commercial product from the specifications also needs a Commercial License.
  4. If you share it or change it, keep the notices, pass on the same license, and give
     recipients the source.
  5. If you use it commercially without a Commercial License, you owe Licensor the amount in
     Section 10 and your rights under this license end.
  6. It is source-available. It is not open source and not free software as those terms
     are defined by the OSI and the FSF.
