1. DEFINITIONS

1.1  "Software" means all computer code in any form in this repository and in every
     repository, package or archive that carries this license: source code, object code,
     scripts, workflows, schemas, migrations, configuration, infrastructure-as-code,
     tests and examples.
1.2  "Specifications" means all architectural specifications, charters, designs,
     protocols, schemas, diagrams, policies, role definitions, doctrine files, templates,
     prompts, documentation and other non-code material that carries this license,
     including the material under specs/ and docs/.
1.3  "Materials" means the Software and the Specifications together, in any medium.
1.4  "Licensor" is the person or entity named in the copyright line above and its
     successors and assigns.
1.5  "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license.
     If You act for or on behalf of an entity, "You" includes that entity and its
     Affiliates. "Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is
     under common control with another entity ("control" means ownership of more than 50%
     of voting interests or the power to direct management).
1.6  "Modification" means any change to the Materials, any translation or adaptation of
     them, and any new work that contains or is derived from a substantial portion of
     them. A separate work that You write without copying from the Materials is not a
     Modification merely because it calls, imports, links to or communicates with the
     Software through a documented interface.
1.7  "Covered Files" means the Materials and all Modifications.
1.8  "Larger Work" means a work that combines Covered Files with files that are not
     Covered Files.
1.9  "Implementation" means any software, system, service, product or process whose
     design, structure or behavior You derive in whole or in part by using the
     Specifications, whether or not it copies any Software.
1.10 "Distribute" means to make a copy of the Materials, a Modification or a Larger Work
     available to any person other than You, by any means, including publishing a
     repository, package, container image or download.
1.11 "Network Use" means letting any person other than You interact with the Software, a
     Modification, an Implementation or a Larger Work remotely over a network.
1.12 "Revenue" means all money and other value, of any kind, that You or any Affiliate
     receives, earns, saves, accrues or is owed, directly or indirectly, from a Commercial
     Use, including sales, subscriptions, usage fees, support and consulting fees,
     advertising, data sales, grants and investment attributable to it, acquisition
     price, cost savings, and the fair market value of non-monetary consideration. It is
     measured gross, without deduction for costs, expenses, taxes or overhead.
1.13 "Commercial License" means a written agreement signed or accepted by Licensor under
     Section 4. Silence, delay, a draft, a quotation, a negotiation or the lack of an
     answer from Licensor is never a Commercial License.
1.14 "Contribution" means anything You submit to Licensor for inclusion in the Materials,
     including a pull request, patch, issue attachment or comment.
1.15 "Output" means data and results that the Software produces for You from Your inputs.

2. GRANT FOR NON-COMMERCIAL USE

2.1  Subject to this license, Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive,
     non-transferable, non-sublicensable license, for the full term of the underlying
     rights, to use, run, copy, study, modify and Distribute the Materials, in source or
     object form, and to build and run Implementations, solely for Non-Commercial Use.
2.2  Each person who receives the Materials from You receives this license directly from
     Licensor on the same terms. You cannot grant more rights than You hold.
2.3  "Non-Commercial Use" means a use that is not a Commercial Use under Section 3.
     The uses in Section 3.3 are Non-Commercial Use.
2.4  Licensor claims no ownership of Your own data or of Your Output. The restriction in
     Section 3 applies to how the Materials are used, not to who owns Your Output.
2.5  Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license under every
     patent claim that Licensor owns or controls, now or later, and that is necessarily
     infringed by the Software as Licensor distributes it, solely for Non-Commercial Use.
     Nothing in this license grants a patent license for Commercial Use. If You start a
     lawsuit, arbitration or other proceeding alleging that the Materials infringe a
     patent, every license in this license ends for You on the date the claim is filed.
     At the date of this version Licensor has filed no patent application on the
     Materials and states no patent rights beyond those that may exist by operation of law.

3. COMMERCIAL USE REQUIRES A COMMERCIAL LICENSE

3.1  The test. Any use of the Materials that makes money, is intended to make money, saves
     money, or forms part of the operations of a for-profit person or organization is a
     "Commercial Use". Commercial Use is not granted by Section 2 and requires a
     Commercial License. This is so wherever You are, wherever the use takes place and
     wherever Your customers are.
3.2  Commercial Use includes, without limitation:
     (a) selling, renting, leasing, licensing or sublicensing the Materials or a
         Modification, or charging for access, downloads, installation, hosting, support
         or training;
     (b) offering the Materials, a Modification, an Implementation, or functionality
         substantially provided by any of them, as or inside a paid or monetized product,
         application, API, platform or hosted service (software-as-a-service), including
         a free product or tier that is monetized by advertising, data collection,
         upselling, subscriptions or investment;
     (c) using the Materials to produce deliverables, results or services for which You or
         anyone else is paid, including consulting, contracting, agency and freelance work;
     (d) any use by or for a for-profit entity or its Affiliates, including internal
         operations, research and development, evaluation, testing and employee training;
     (e) running a business, a company, a product line or an organization of any kind
         with the Materials, or using the Materials to start, operate or improve any
         activity that produces Revenue;
     (f) building, selling, offering or operating an Implementation of the Specifications
         for any of the purposes in (a) to (e), or an Implementation that competes with
         the Software as a paid product or service;
     (g) embedding or bundling the Materials in hardware, devices or other products that
         are sold or leased;
     (h) using the Materials, their source code or their Output to train, fine-tune,
         distill or evaluate any artificial-intelligence, machine-learning or
         code-generation model, system or service that is offered commercially or that
         is used in a Commercial Use, however the activity is described legally (for
         example "text and data mining", "intermediate copying" or "fair use");
     (i) scraping, crawling or bulk-downloading the Materials to build datasets, indexes
         or products that are used in a Commercial Use; and
     (j) any other use in which the Materials contribute to Revenue, investment value,
         market position or cost savings for any person or organization.
3.3  Non-Commercial Use. The following are Non-Commercial Use, provided no part of
     Section 3.2 applies to the same activity:
     (a) personal use by an individual who earns no money from it;
     (b) teaching, study and education;
     (c) academic or scientific research whose results are published or otherwise made
         publicly available;
     (d) use by a registered non-profit organization, an educational institution or a
         government body for its public mission; and
     (e) building and running a project or community that is itself free of charge and
         unmonetized.
     Grants, donations and tuition that fund these activities are not Revenue from the
     Materials, provided the Materials are not themselves sold, licensed, hosted for a fee
     or made the paid component of a product, service or deliverable. A user in (a) to (e)
     who later does anything described in Section 3.2 needs a Commercial License for it.
3.4  Mixed use and Affiliates. If a use is partly commercial, the whole use is Commercial
     Use. A for-profit entity cannot use a non-profit, student, individual or Affiliate as a
     conduit. Splitting, routing or renaming an activity to avoid Section 3 is a breach.
3.5  Dual purpose. The Software may be used to operate a business that its operator runs
     for someone else (for example a client). Doing so for pay is Commercial Use under
     Section 3.2(c).
3.6  The Materials are a method and a codebase. A Commercial License is needed whether You
     use the Software itself, a Modification, or an Implementation You wrote after studying
     the Specifications. Section 3.7 describes what is outside this license.
3.7  Outside this license. Licensor makes no claim over (a) ideas, methods, facts or
     general knowledge that You hold independently of the Materials, (b) software You
     develop without access to the Specifications or the Software, and (c) any use that
     applicable law allows regardless of license terms. This license is a contract that
     binds You when You access, copy, use or build on the Materials. It does not remove
     any right that mandatory law gives You.

4. COMMERCIAL LICENSE; REVENUE SHARE

4.1  Licensor offers Commercial Licenses by separate written agreement. Standard terms,
     including the default revenue share, are published in COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md and may
     change for future agreements. Licensor may grant, refuse or condition a Commercial
     License at its sole discretion, and may offer different terms to different persons.
4.2  A Commercial License may take any of these forms: revenue-share license; fixed-fee
     license; time-limited, field-limited or territory-limited license; hybrid license;
     public-benefit or open-source-contribution conditional license; or a custom license.
4.3  The default form is a revenue-share license under which Licensor receives a stated
     percentage of Revenue, reported and paid on a stated schedule, with a right to audit
     records to the extent needed to verify the amount.
4.4  To request a Commercial License, write to the contact in Section 15. Describe the
     intended use, the Materials involved, the expected scale and duration and the
     proposed form. Nothing obliges Licensor to answer, and no answer is an approval.
4.5  Nothing in this license creates an implied commercial license, estoppel, waiver or
     expectation of one. A Commercial Use that starts before a Commercial License is
     signed is an unlicensed use under Section 10.
4.6  An entity that already has a Commercial License is bound by that agreement for the use
     it covers. Where the agreement is silent, this license applies.

5. SHARING, SOURCE AND NOTICES (RECIPROCITY)

If You Distribute the Materials, a Modification or a Larger Work, then:
5.1  Same license. You must Distribute the Covered Files only under this license (this
     version or a later version issued by Licensor).
5.2  Source. You must make the complete source of the Covered Files You Distribute
     available to every recipient free of charge, for as long as You Distribute them,
     either with the distribution or by a written notice with a working link.
5.3  Notices. You must keep intact all copyright notices, SPDX headers, this LICENSE and
     any NOTICE file, and state with the date in each changed file that You changed it.
5.4  Attribution. You must credit "Ultrastable" and its Licensor, link to this license, and
     indicate changes, in reasonable form for the medium. Where You document or describe
     an Implementation of the Specifications, say that it implements the Ultrastable
     specifications.
5.5  Larger Works. Files in a Larger Work that are not Covered Files may carry Your own
     terms. Those terms may not purport to grant rights in the Covered Files, and Section 3
     applies to every use of the Larger Work in which Covered Files are used.
5.6  Network Use. If You modify the Software and offer it for Network Use, You must offer
     each user the source of Your Modification under this license through a prominent link
     in the interface or the API documentation.
5.7  No further restrictions. You may not add restrictions on a recipient's exercise of the
     rights this license grants, and You may not use technical measures to prevent
     recipients from modifying or rebuilding the Covered Files.

6. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Components that Licensor did not write remain under their own licenses, which You must
follow. They are listed in package manifests or a NOTICE file where distributed. If a
third-party license conflicts with this license, it governs that component only. Because
this license restricts commercial use, Covered Files may not be combined with software under
the GNU GPL, LGPL or AGPL in any way that would require the combination to be distributed
under those licenses.

7. CONTRIBUTIONS

By submitting a Contribution You (a) certify that You have the right to submit it, as in the
Developer Certificate of Origin 1.1 (https://developercertificate.org/); (b) license it to
everyone under this license; (c) grant Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free, irrevocable license, including under any patent claims You own or control that
read on the Contribution, to use, modify, Distribute and sublicense it on any terms,
including in Commercial Licenses; and (d) keep Your copyright in it. Licensor need not accept
any Contribution. This lets Licensor offer one Commercial License covering the whole work.

8. NAMES AND MARKS

This license grants no right to use the names "Ultrastable", "QNFO" or "QWAV", their logos
or other marks, domains or social handles, except to state accurately where the Materials
