9. NO WARRANTY ON WHAT THE SOFTWARE DECIDES

The Materials describe and operate autonomous agents. They may contain defects and may act in
ways You did not expect. They are not designed, tested or certified for safety-critical,
medical, legal, financial or other high-risk decisions. You are responsible for verifying any
result before relying on it and for the actions Your own deployment takes.

10. UNLICENSED COMMERCIAL USE; BREACH; TERMINATION

10.1 If You make a Commercial Use without a Commercial License, then, in addition to Licensor's
     other remedies: (a) Your rights under this license end automatically for the Materials
     involved, from the first day of the unlicensed use; (b) You must stop the Commercial Use
     within 14 days of notice; and (c) You agree to pay Licensor, as liquidated damages, an
     amount equal to eighty-five percent (85%) of all Revenue derived directly or indirectly
     from that use. The parties agree that Licensor's actual damages are very hard to
     measure, because the Materials are intangible and copied cheaply, the benefit of using
     them is spread through a business, and distribution is global. They agree that this
     amount is a reasonable pre-estimate of the damages and not a penalty. [ATTORNEY REVIEW:
     percentage and enforceability by jurisdiction; see docs/legal/LICENSE-REVIEW.md.]
10.2 Fallback. If a court or arbitral tribunal holds the amount in Section 10.1 unenforceable
     in whole or part (for example as a penalty, under Article 163(3) of the Swiss Code of
     Obligations, under sections 343 and 339 to 345 of the German Civil Code or under a
     similar rule), then Licensor may instead recover, at Licensor's election: (a) the highest
     amount that the tribunal finds enforceable, up to 85% of Revenue; or (b) actual damages,
     statutory or enhanced damages where available (for example 17 U.S.C. section 504), the
     infringer's profits attributable to the use, a reasonable royalty of not less than the
     published standard rate under Section 4.3, and Licensor's reasonable legal, expert and
     investigation costs. Licensor may also obtain an injunction and an accounting.
10.3 Other breaches. If Your only breach is of Section 5 (notices, attribution, source or
     Network Use) and not of Section 3, Your license is reinstated if You cure the breach
     within 30 days after You first become aware of it. This is available once. A breach of
     Section 3 has no cure period.
10.4 Termination also follows from the patent claim in Section 2.5 and from a final decision
     that You infringed Licensor's rights outside this license. Licenses of recipients who
     got the Materials from You in compliance with this license stay in force.
10.5 Licensor and its successors may enforce this license, and the copyright and other rights
     in the Materials, in any lawful way, including through platform take-down procedures
     (such as the DMCA and equivalent regimes), payment processors, hosting providers and
     package registries.
10.6 Sections 1, 3, 4.5, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14 survive termination.

