11.1 This license is governed by the substantive law of Switzerland, excluding its conflict of
     laws rules and excluding the United Nations Convention on Contracts for the
     International Sale of Goods. Switzerland is chosen as a neutral law that is accessible
     to parties from every region.
11.2 Any dispute arising out of or relating to this license, including its validity,
     interpretation, breach or termination, is finally resolved by arbitration under the
     Arbitration Rules of the International Chamber of Commerce by one arbitrator. The seat is
     Geneva, Switzerland. The language is English. The award is final and binding and may be
     enforced in any court that has jurisdiction, in particular under the New York Convention
     of 1958.
11.3 Either party may at any time apply to any court of competent jurisdiction for interim,
     conservatory or injunctive relief, and Licensor may enforce its intellectual-property
     rights in any court where the use occurs.
11.4 Local law. You must follow all laws that apply to You where You use the Materials,
     including export-control, sanctions and data-protection law. Where mandatory local law
     gives Licensor stronger protection, that protection applies. Where mandatory local law
     limits a provision of this license, the provision applies to the maximum extent the
     law allows, and the rest of this license is not affected.
11.5 No consumer protection is removed. Nothing in this license removes a right that
     mandatory consumer-protection law gives a natural person who uses the Materials for
     personal, non-commercial purposes.

